config BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_COMPUTE_INTEL
	bool "Intel GPU/XPU compute host contract (i915/xe + firmware + dri nodes)"
	default y if BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_GPU_AI_ALL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE
	help
	  Establishes the HOST side of Intel GPU compute:

	    * i915 / xe kernel drivers   (enabled via the kernel fragment)
	    * Intel GuC/HuC + DMC firmware (from linux-firmware)
	    * /dev/dri/renderD* nodes with the correct permissions (udev overlay)

	  It deliberately does NOT compile intel-compute-runtime (NEO), the Intel
	  Graphics Compiler (IGC), gmmlib, or level-zero into the base OS. That
	  stack (a) is impractical to cross-compile in Buildroot - IGC alone drags
	  in LLVM/Clang/SPIRV - and (b) does not belong in an immutable appliance
	  rootfs. The Level-Zero / oneAPI / NEO runtime ships in the add-on
	  container (Intel publishes oneAPI base images), talking to the kernel
	  driver through the /dev/dri render node this contract guarantees.

	  See NOTES.md in this package directory for the container-side recipe.
